== A. Prop 4.1(b), d = 2: exact range of x_r over sign vectors vs the zonotope half-width
   600 (matrix, r <= 4, coordinate) cases: extreme values = +-h_{r,i} exactly in all but 0

== B. Prop 4.1(c): horizon r*(delta) exact vs the closed forms (e_0 = 0)
   2015 (L, delta/eps) cells: 0 mismatches (closed forms in floating point with a 1e-12 guard; contraction-limit test exact)
   delta/eps = 10^4, L = 1: r* = 10000
   delta/eps = 10^4, L = 101/100: r* = 463
   delta/eps = 10^4, L = 11/10: r* = 72
   delta/eps = 10^4, L = 2: r* = 13

== C. scope: a nonlinear F with Lipschitz constant 2, F(x) = 0 on [-1,1], F(x) = 2(x - sign(x)) outside
   exact width/2 of the set of x_r over the models: {'1/10'} for every r = 1..30
   record's e_r (L = 2): r=1: 1/10, r=5: 31/10, r=30: 1073741823/10; so at precision delta = 1/10 the formula's horizon is r* = 1, yet the honest law proves 'x_r in [-1/10, 1/10]' (centred at F^r(a) = 0) at every depth r

== D. Prop 4.3(c): Helly in dimension 1 (exhaustive), boxes, discs
   all 12628 families of 2-4 closed integer intervals in [0,5]: pairwise <=> joint fails in 0
   20000 random families of 2-5 integer boxes in the plane: pairwise <=> joint fails in 0
   discs of radius 1.1 at the vertices of an equilateral triangle of side 2: pairwise distance 2 <= 2.2; circumradius^2 = 4/3 = 1.3333 > 1.21 = 1.1^2, so no common point (exact)

== E. Remark 4.4: typical against worst case
   r = 100, random signs +-eps: E|S_r| = r C(r, r/2) 2^-r = 7.9589 eps (sqrt(2r/pi) = 7.9788); worst case 100 eps
   r = 1000, random signs +-eps: E|S_r| = r C(r, r/2) 2^-r = 25.2250 eps (sqrt(2r/pi) = 25.2313); worst case 1000 eps
   r = 100, errors uniform on [-eps, eps]: E|S| = 4.611 eps (record about 4.6)
   L = 1.1, r = 100: worst case 1.378e+05 eps (record 1.38e5); random signs: E|.| ~ sqrt(2/pi) * 3.007e+04 = 2.399e+04 eps (Gaussian approximation; record about 2.4e4)
   L = 1.1, r = 100, random signs, Monte Carlo (10^6 draws, seeded): E|.| = 2.422e+04 eps

